	abstract = {Large language models (LLMs) such as OpenAI Codex and GPT-4 have catalyzed the development of AI-powered code generation tools like GitHub Copilot, ChatGPT, and Amazon CodeWhisperer. This paper presents a systematic survey of recent research exploring the implications of AI-generated code on software development, with particular attention to accuracy, security vulnerabilities, and developer trust. We synthesize findings from peer-reviewed studies, industry evaluations, and technical whitepapers, identifying strengths, limitations, and areas for improvement. Our review highlights key trade-offs between productivity and safety, outlines recurring vulnerability patterns, and discusses the evolving relationship between developers and AI systems. We conclude with a call for human-in-the-loop design, explainable AI interfaces, and more rigorous benchmarks to evaluate the reliability of AI-generated code in real-world scenarios.},
