	doi = {10.1007/978-981-96-8104-4_50},
	abstract = {The integration of machine learning (ML) in software engineering has revolutionized the software development lifecycle, automating critical processes such as code generation, testing, bug detection, and performance optimization. This paper explores the advanced ML techniques that are emerging in software engineering, including deep learning, reinforcement learning, and federated learning, and examines their impact on improving software quality, scalability, and efficiency. Through a detailed analysis of real-world case studies, we demonstrate how these advanced methods outperform traditional approaches in key areas like predictive maintenance, anomaly detection, and project management. Additionally, we address the challenges and ethical considerations surrounding the use of ML in software engineering, particularly in terms of model interpretability, data privacy, and scalability. Finally, we outline future research directions and discuss the potential of quantum computing and AI-driven automation to further transform software engineering. This paper provides valuable insights for practitioners and researchers seeking to leverage cutting-edge ML techniques to enhance software development practices. {\textcopyright} The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2026.},
