	doi = {10.11959/j.issn.2096-109x.2026009},
	abstract = {Automatic program repair (APR) technology holds a significant position in the field of software engineering, but existing large language model based APR methods suffer from significant limitations in search localization, execution efficiency, and cost control. To address these issues, an adaptive program repair system named AutoVulnFix based on lightweight intelligent search was proposed. This system resolved the existing problems through three core technologies: a simplified prompt strategy, a dual-track intelligent search algorithm, and multi-level cache. Specifically, it first reduced token costs by intelligent context management and precise problem description, then enhanced the system's response speed through delayed loading and intelligent caching strategies, and finally combined a fast search track and an intelligent search track to adaptively select the optimal search strategy based on task complexity. A comprehensive comparative evaluation was conducted on five large language models using a dataset containing 231 code defect samples. Experimental results demonstrate that AutoVulnFix achieves an average improvement of 4.2 percentage points in repair accuracy, an average reduction of 25.8\% in execution time, and an average saving of 21.4\% in token consumption. The system provides an effective solution for practical deployment of APR technology. {\textcopyright} 2026 Beijing Xintong Media Co., Ltd.. All rights reserved.},
