	abstract = {In group software projects, individual contributions often vary significantly, but detecting imbalances is time-consuming and complex. This research project examines how Large Language Models (LLMs) can aid in validating student contributions by analysing self-reports and Git histories. We developed a prototype tool that automatically extracts coding-related claims, locates corresponding commits, and verifies supporting evidence. Evaluation across two course cohorts shows the tool achieves high claim validation precision (0.94); however, it is stricter than human reviewers in its requirement for explicit evidence. {\textcopyright} 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)},
