	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105036242869?origin=resultslist},
	doi = {10.1016/j.ijhydene.2026.154965},
	abstract = {Active, stable, and low-cost alkaline oxygen evolution reaction (OER) catalyst is essential for large-scale hydrogen (H2) production via electrochemical water splitting. Traditional catalyst design often relies on experience-driven, trial-and-error approaches, limits exploration efficiency. To overcome this, we present an artificial intelligence (AI)-assisted high-throughput framework combining large language models (LLMs)-based literature mining and Python-driven simulations. LLMs identifies FeNi-layered double hydroxide (FeNi-LDH) has excellent activity for OER while Python-based simulations propose a needle-like facilitate bubble detachment. In our experimental, the as-prepared FeNi-LDH exhibits good OER activity (237~mV at 10~mA~cm-2). After growing FeNi-LDH on NiTe array, the needle-like FeNi-LDH-NiTe not only delivers enhanced activity (198~mV at 10~mA~cm-2), but also exhibits faster bubble generation and migration, which allow it to stably work at high current density (1~A~cm-2). The successful AI-guided catalyst design proposes a clear strategy to decouple kinetic and non-kinetic optimization for exploring excellent electrocatalyst. {\textcopyright} 2026 Hydrogen Energy Publications LLC. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
