	abstract = {This research addresses the critical gap between AI's potential and its practical integration into software engineering (SE) education. We propose a novel educational framework using project-based learning to embed AI tools across the SE lifecycle. Thirty capstone students participated in a workshop to automate a requirements-to-code workflow using a toolchain of AI agents and development platforms, incorporating a human-in-the-loop for validation. Motivation and learning were assessed through pre- and post-intervention surveys using the ARCS model. This study provides a practical framework for SE education, emphasizing critical AI evaluation and strategic tool use. Pending findings will offer insights into preparing a workforce for effective human-AI collaboration, with future work focusing on data analysis and scaling the intervention. {\textcopyright} 2025 IEEE.},
