	isbn = {979-833157605-9 (ISBN)},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105028906213?origin=resultslist},
	doi = {10.1109/EIT67313.2025.11232327},
	abstract = {Modern radar systems predominantly utilize multicore digital signal processors. To fully exploit hardware capabilities, software implementations must adopt parallelized designs, at the same time, existing serial code must be ported to parallel architectures. However, manual parallelization - whether through de novo development or code transformation - exhibits signficantly diminished productivity. More critically, the architectural heterogeneity prevalent among radar computing platforms and operating systems compels the maintenance of multiple parallel implementations for algorithmically equivalent functions, thereby substantially compromising development efficiency in radar software ecosystems. This paper presents an automatic parallel program generation framework for radar signal processing systems, featuring full compatibility with OpenMP standards. Our methodology involves: (1) constructing a parallel primitive annotation model, (2) developing directive-based code marking techniques for sequential programs, and (3) implementing a compiler-assisted transformation tool that automatically converts annotated serial code into optimized parallel implementations. Extensive benchmarking was performed across diverse radar operating environments including Kylin, Reworks, SylixOS, and Linux platforms. Experimental results demonstrate that the auto-generated parallel code achieves 90\% of the performance efficiency of manually optimized OpenMP/multi-threaded implementations, while delivering a 3{\texttimes} improvement in parallel software development productivity.  {\textcopyright} 2025 IEEE.},
	language = {English},
	booktitle = {Int. {Conf}. {Electron}. {Inf}. {Technol}., {EIT}},
	publisher = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.},
